<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pi-Ramesses</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Per-Ramesses, Piramesse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pi-Ramesses was the capital built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a>, at modern Qantir, on the site of the older city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>. It held palaces, temples, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> workshops and barracks for campaigns into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. When the branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> beside it silted up around the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, it was abandoned, and many of its statues and blocks were carried to the new capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pi-ramesses.jpg" alt="Pi-Ramesses" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iri-en-achti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kolossalstatue_Qantir.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
